[38;2;124;124;124mLet me think about this carefully.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mA symplectic submanifold of (M, ω) is a submanifold N ⊆ M such that the [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mrestriction of ω to N is symplectic (i.e., closed and non-degenerate on N).[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mWait, let me be careful about definitions. There are different notions. A [0m
[38;2;124;124;124m"symplectic submanifold" typically means a submanifold N such that ω|_N is a [0m
[38;2;124;124;124msymplectic form on N. This requires:[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m1. ω|_N is closed (automatic since d(ω|_N) = (dω)|_N = 0)[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m2. ω|_N is non-degenerate on N, i.e., for every p ∈ N, the map T_p N → T*_p N [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mgiven by v ↦ ω_p(v, ·) is injective. Equivalently, T_p N ∩ (T_p N)^ω = {0} where[0m[38;2;124;124;124m(T_p N)^ω is the symplectic orthogonal.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mSo N is symplectic iff T_p N is a symplectic subspace of (T_p M, ω_p) for all p [0m[38;2;124;124;124m∈ N, i.e., N is a symplectic subspace at each point.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mNow, an open subset U of M: T_p U = T_p M for all p ∈ U (since U is open, the [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mtangent space is the same). So ω|_U restricted to T_p U = T_p M is just ω_p [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mitself, which is non-degenerate. And closedness is automatic.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mSo yes, any open subset U of M, with the restricted form ω|_U, is a symplectic [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mmanifold. And as a submanifold, U is an open submanifold, and the inclusion is [0m
